    "Pennisi MG, Cardoso L, Baneth G, et al. •Dogs—meglumine antimoniate (100 mg/kg SC q24h or 50–75 mg/kg SC q12h for 1 month) or miltefosine (2 mg/kg PO q24h for 1 month). Best in combination with long-term",
    "Solano-Gallego L, Miró G, Koutinas A, et al. allopurinol (10 mg/kg PO q12h for 12–24 months). Allopurinol may also be used alone. • Cats—allopurinol (10 mg/kg PO q12–24h) as monotherapy. Short-term meglumine"
  ],
