    "author": "sLaia Solano-Gallego and Gad antimoniate (20–50 mg/kg SC q24h) plus Baneth allopurinol is optional.",
    "consulting_editor": "Amie Koenig",
    "acknowledgment": "The authors and editors acknowledge the prior contribution of Stephen C. Barr. FOLLOW-UP PATIENT MONITORING •Monitor clinical signs, laboratory abnormalities, and antibody levels (quantitative serology) at day 30, 90, 180 and then every 6 months. • Relapses (rise in antibody or globulin concentrations and/or reappearance of clinical signs, laboratory abnormalities) may occur months to years after therapy or during therapy if drug resistance develops; recheck at least every 2 months after treatment completion. Drug resistance reported for allopurinol. • Monitor for urolithiasis and renal mineralization in dogs on long-term allopurinol. MISCELLANEOUS LeishVet update and recommendations on feline leishmaniosis. Parasit Vectors 2015, 8:302. LeishVet guidelines for the practical management of canine leishmaniosis. Parasit. Vectors 2011, 4:86."
